{{!
    @template block_compass/block

    The block shell: a React mount point for tier 1 and, beside it, the region tier 3
    still renders into.

    Tier 3 is an AMD module until phase R3, and it writes its markup into
    data-region="explore" directly. That region is therefore a SIBLING of the mount
    point, outside React's tree: rendered from the component, React would own it and
    undo explore.js's work on the next render. It moves inside when tier 3 does.

    The props arrive already JSON-encoded from the renderable, in one value, through a
    triple stash - the same shape phase R1 arrived at, and for the same reason: the
    quote helper corrupts any value carrying a doubled-brace pair, and JSON.stringify
    in the producer does not. Nothing between here and React is an HTML context, so a
    double stash would reach the reader as literal entities.

    The section's trailing content is what a reader sees if the component never
    mounts, which is silent apart from a console message. It says the block could not
    load, which is then true, and offers nothing to press. Only the mounted component
    renders course cards, so a step asserting a course name asserts that React ran.

    The noscript beside it covers the other way this block shows nothing. With
    JavaScript off both messages appear, and both are true: one says what happened,
    the other says why.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON-encoded by block_compass\output\block:
      labels, icons, strips, favouritesenabled, showsearch and showindex.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"labels\": {\"loaderror\": \"Your courses could not be loaded.\"}, \"strips\": []}"
    }
}}
<div class="compass-root" data-region="block_compass">
    {{#react}}
    {
        "component": "@moodle/lms/block_compass/Block",
        "props": {{{props}}}
    }
    <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}loaderror, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    {{/react}}
    <div class="compass-explore-wrap mt-3" data-region="explore" hidden></div>
    <noscript>
        <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}javascriptrequired, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    </noscript>
</div>
